Every line of the header block above is wrong in a different way, and a
parser is expected to recover from all of them: keep what it can parse,
discard what it cannot, and never fail the message. Note in particular
the duplicate Subject (the first occurrence wins), the unparseable Date
(fall back to the Received date or to the internal date), and the empty
boundary parameter on a non-multipart Content-Type.
